{
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Nationals of Austria, Belgium, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Portugal, Spain and Sweden, and EFTA states (Iceland, Liechtenstein, Norway) get a C permit after 5 years' regular, uninterrupted residence under settlement treaties.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Other EU states have no such treaty.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant contradicts the provided reference by asserting that the 5-year residence criterion applies only to specific countries with bilateral agreements, rather than to the listed EU and EFTA states under settlement treaties as stated in the reference. This misrepresentation of the legal basis constitutes a factual contradiction.",
  "evidence": "The assistant claims \"For nationals of specific countries (typically those with which France has signed agreements or bilateral arrangements), this 5-year uninterrupted residence period may qualify them for a C permit...\" which directly contradicts the reference stating that nationals of the listed countries get a C permit after 5 years under settlement treaties."
}
